2026-07-05 16:46:08.843 | INFO     | app.services.set_service:get_text_for_set:244 - [GET TEXT] Final result text: Every summer, Lina would venture beyond the city, eager to practice her agile mind and legs.  
She believed whatever path she chose could improve her life if she kept moving.  
At dawn, she would dwell beside the river, watching ever-changing light on the water.  
The quiet made her feel that every small venture could become an everlasting memory.  
So she trained with steady practice, running over rocks and through wet grass.  
Her steps grew more agile, and her breathing improved with every bright morning.  
Whatever storms came, she kept going, certain that effort would improve her future.  
She returned often to the river, where birds seemed to dwell in everlasting peace.  
There, she planned her next venture, ready to practice patience and courage again.  
By autumn, Lina felt ever stronger, agile in body and heart, and prepared for whatever came.
